{
 "source": "look-behinds over supplementary characters. Behind/NotBehind (the pattern from the look-behind to its end holds no supplementary character) step back one UTF-16 unit at a time and read codePointAt from there, a lone low surrogate when the start falls between a pair's halves (\\p{Cs}, ., [^a] right after a supplementary character; (?<=\\x{1F600}) never holds); BehindS/NotBehindS step back by code points and read the whole pair, also from a search started between the surrogates (a-?-- for (?<=a)|.(?<=😀) over a😀😀). replaceAll, Matcher.find ($regex.matches) and matches() (a REGEX body matcher)",
